messages "guest**To: sauronSubj: languagesCc: cigaretta, guestDate: Dec  9Hi Sauron! I'm Cigaretta. I'm an old player here, this is a new character.I played today. A few guys were releasing latin sayings through thechat line. just because it sounded good, maybe they didn't even know what they meant. then figleaf comes: chat line is english only.you know, this rule has gone a little too far. many people here are notnative english, and i myself don't get harrassed if someone speaks a language that i don't understand, but i'll try to understand that others do.however, what happened today is that after figleaf came with englishonly, others including myself started to say things through the line. like \"argelbargel kalahu\", which means nothing.figleaf then jailed 2 of us. jailed me after my question: wo ist das Jail?something is wrong here. i get the rules, but it's an abuse of power. wedon't come here to play in a police state.not to mention another case: i was talking to a good friend in hungarian.then i realized that someone was standing on our square. i saw stiletto was on.so we rushed to the church (we don't have a house). and continued there.then stiletto complained to exos that we speak a \"foreign language\" in a public room. exos came and forbade us. all of this is going too far.i speak 4 languages, and i feel that i have the right to speak any ofthem whenever i want to. if many are bugged by it, ok, i won't, but itshouldn't go beyond rational measures. I'm not sure about the solution.It would be great for instance to have a twin brother of the chat linethat is international (that's easy to code, I guess).In short, this disorganized letter is asking you to do something about the problem.I ask you as someone I find most cooperative and rational.I represent the opinion of several people.Regards:Cigaretta**"
